{"name":"Elite Wisteria","hex":"#987fa9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of high birth or social position; aristocratic or patrician.","Representing the choicest or most select of a group."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A special group or social class of people who have a superior social or economic status and attendant power, advantages, or privileges in society; a member of such a group.","An individual member of such a group."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elite"},{"term":"wisteria","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several woody climbing vines, of the genus Wisteria, native to the East Asian countries of China, Korea, and Japan and the eastern United States.","The lavenderish color of their flowers; specifically:"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wisteria"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elite","blocks":[{"text":"In political and sociological theory, the elite are a small group of powerful or wealthy people who hold a disproportionate amount of wealth, privilege, political power, or skill in a group. Defined by the Cambridge Dictionary, the \"elite\" are \"the richest, most powerful, best-educated, or best-trained group in a society\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Prime_Minister_Boris_Johnson_UNGA_visit_%2851786182369%29.jpg/330px-Prime_Minister_Boris_Johnson_UNGA_visit_%2851786182369%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elite"},{"title":"Wisteria","blocks":[{"text":"Wisteria is a genus of flowering plants in the legume family, Fabaceae (Leguminosae). The genus includes four species of woody twining vines that are native to China, Japan, Korea, Vietnam, southern Canada, the Eastern United States, and north of Iran. They were later introduced to England, France, Germany and various other countries in Europe. Some species are popular ornamental plants. The genus name is also used as the English name, and may then be spelt 'wistaria'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Chinese_Wisteria_Bl%C3%BCtentrauben.JPG/330px-Chinese_Wisteria_Bl%C3%BCtentrauben.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wisteria"},{"title":"Lavender (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lavender is a light shade of purple or violet. It applies particularly to the color of the flower of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Lavandula_fields.jpg/330px-Lavandula_fields.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavender_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg/500px-Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg/1280px-Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg/500px-Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bill Clinton (left middle),[21][22] Jeffrey Epstein (right middle),[21][22][23][24] and Ghislaine Maxwell (right)[21] have been characterized as associating with the global elite.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Demo-gegen-wef.jpg/500px-Demo-gegen-wef.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Demo-gegen-wef.jpg/1280px-Demo-gegen-wef.jpg?